  "uses_meanings": {
   "ledger": "The wallet's result in this vault is the result key: what it took home on the money it withdrew, from the vault's public ledger.",
   "list": "The wallet's result in this vault is the listed_result key: its all-time result on the venue's own depositor list."
  },
  "status_meanings": {
   "left": "The wallet withdrew and the venue does not list it with money inside.",
   "withdrew, may still be inside": "The wallet withdrew and is not on the venue's list. The list stops at 100 names and wallets beyond it can hold money in this vault, so this wallet may still have money inside that is not shown."
  },
  "cannot_see": [
   "A wallet that deposited, never withdrew and is not on the venue's list. The list can stop at 100 names. It then appears to show the largest balances, so smaller depositors who never withdrew are the ones missing.",
   "What a payout paid to a wallet that is not on the list. A payout is one sum in the ledger.",
   "Deposits. A deposit row does not name the depositor, so a wallet's cost is known only for money it withdrew.",
   "Vaults that are not covered: those whose books do not add up, the venue's own vaults (no ledger on file) and open vaults the daily capture holds no details for (under $1,000 inside).",
   "For a leader, the cuts it collected from depositors. They leave the vault and are not in the leader's figures.",
   "A wallet that was left out of these files on request. The counts say how many were left out, never which."
  ]
